From 3bb9f2aed8bf86eb9d94f71a7334f974f6b8f89c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 18:59:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 56/58] topk: in-kernel canonical emission
 (MERLIN_TOPK_SORTED_EMIT)

Emits the selected indices in canonical ascending order inside the kernel so
the Python QSA sort can be skipped. Output-equivalent to the Python sort;
reference model, property tests and GPU arms included. Default off in this
commit.
